THIS IS A RELAUNCH — the first attempt was aborted at 5/126
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attempt 1 (2026-08-17, main @ c1220bc) is frozen at
  results/screening-batch1-aborted-20260817-gatefix/
It is NOT a screening result: container_gate() never mounted the sealed hidden
set, so every run graded acceptance.result: error with the hidden gate reporting
awaiting_human. Real spend, real telemetry, no gradable outcome. $1.8634 billed.

Fixed in PR #21 (merged 2026-08-17): container_gate() mounts the host sealed set
read-only at <task>/hidden and exports HIDDEN_TESTS_DIR; hidden_tests_dir()
resolves the same directory for the host and container gates.
Regression coverage: tests/test_container_gate.py, 9 tests; 5 fail pre-fix.

Pre-approved grading smoke before this relaunch (cap $1, containerized C2 on the
pilot task), results/smoke-gatefix/:
  acceptance.result = accepted
  hidden gate       = pass, sealed-pilot-v1 2026-07-19
  hash              = sha256:105c24189877b52fe57b1e453f53f73366ad3c7fa1a611a8a2a63042b667abe2
                      == the frozen manifest value (exact match)
  cost              = $0.2190618, cost_basis marginal_api_cost, authoritative
So the dependent variable is measurable in this posture before any batch spend.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARED LIMITATION — W6 run summaries stamp hidden_test_hash: null
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Known, accepted and declared by the human before the first attempt (2026-08-17);
carried forward unchanged into this relaunch. NOT affected by the PR #21 fix.

What happens:
  harness/runner/run.py reads the manifest key `sealed_hidden_test` only
  (run.py:478, :485, :892). W6's sealed artifact is a seeded-defect map and is
  carried under a DIFFERENT manifest key, `sealed_defect_map`. run.py therefore
  finds nothing to read for W6 and every W6 run summary in this batch records
    hidden_test_hash: null
  even though W6's artifact IS frozen (sealed-w6-v1 2026-08-17 k=6,
  sha256:350bf452c631dec30b413b422b871c4d974fa4df19adc9668b1d10266b4d1002).

This null is a JOIN GAP, NOT a missing measurement. It must not be read as
"W6 has no sealed artifact" or as an `unavailable` telemetry field: the artifact
is frozen and the gate fingerprints it on every single run. W6 provenance for
this batch is carried by two intact records:
  1. manifest/delivery-manifest.yaml -> w6_task.sealed_defect_map.sha256
     (frozen 2026-08-17, status: frozen)
  2. each W6 run's own gate-hidden.json fingerprint, written by
     harness/task-tools/gate/check-hidden.sh at gate time

Disposition:
  - No runner change for this key mismatch (human decision). It remains open as a
    follow-up; it is a defect in the reader, not in the data.
  - Post-batch, summarize.py joins the hash from each run's gate-hidden.json, so
    the derived tables carry W6 provenance even though the raw run summaries do
    not.

