Why the batch halted (plan index 19, W4 P0 rep1) and what changed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The runner's mid-batch auto-build passed none of the image build args, so images
built after the batch started took the Dockerfile default uid 1001 instead of the
host uid. uid 1001 cannot read the 0600 credential mounts, and the runner refused
(see the halt record at 2026-08-18T04:32:27Z above). Fixed in PR #23: both build
paths now resolve their build args through one function, and a regression test
asserts the built image's recorded uid equals the invoking user's.

Two defects that the uid guard had masked, also fixed in PR #23:
  - the auto-built W4 agent image labelled lab.cli.agy.version=unavailable while
    carrying the vendored binary. Left in, every billed Product-B leg would have
    stamped "unavailable" into identity.product_version. AGY_REQUIRED is now a
    hard build-time assertion.
  - uv was absent from the base image and the uv venv did not survive relocation
    into the agent image, so the three python-stack tasks (W3, W4b, W1b) could
    not be built or imported at all.

All 12 roster images (gate + agent for W4, W1, W4b, W3, W1b, W6) were pre-built
as this user before this relaunch and verified: lab.image.subject_uid=706335951
(= host), lab.cli.agy.version=1.1.13, lab.cli.claude.version=2.1.233. No image is
built mid-batch in this pass.

