3. LIMITATION — W1 HIDDEN-GATE REJECTS ARE AN INSTRUMENT ERROR, NOT A RESULT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLASSIFICATION: (a) instrument error. The W1 rejects are NOT evidence that the
agents wrote weak tests. Read-only forensic, no gate change, no cell skipped.

Observation. All 16 W1 cells run so far are acceptance.result=rejected. 15 of them
record hidden={"status":"fail"} at sealed-w1-v1 2026-07-20 6-mutants,
sha256:37f3acd6...c51f4e9; the 16th (C5 rep1) has no hidden block. Every one of
them PASSED the full public gate first:
    T1-diff-scope   pass  only new test files under src/tests/
    T2-suite-green  pass  baseline suite (article|profile|utils|tag|mapper)
    T3-coverage     pass  article.mapper.ts 0/0=100.0%; author.mapper.ts 5/6=83.33%
    T4-tests-pass   pass  agent's new tests pass on the pinned target files
So the agent's test file existed, was discovered, executed, and hit the reachable
branch ceiling exactly. A "no agent test file / discovery broke" story is already
inconsistent with T1-T4 passing in the SAME container.

Decisive check. The agent's own output for W1 P0 rep1 is stored in that run dir as
agent-solution.diff. Applied to the pinned tree and graded with the SAME sealed
runner at the SAME hash and version, on the host:
    == hidden gate (w1-realworld-mapper-tests) [test_generation] ==
      version: sealed-w1-v1 2026-07-20 6-mutants
      hash:    sha256:37f3acd685fd03e0624a98f328e38edffe8faef5179263e502035c707c51f4e9
      -- sealed runner (stderr) --
      | hidden: caught: m1 ... m6   (all six mutant ids caught)
      | hidden: all 6 mutants caught
    == hidden gate: PASS ==   (exit 0)
Same agent output, same sealed runner, same hash: PASS on the host, FAIL in the
container. The tests genuinely catch every mutant. The in-container verdict is
false. The work tree was restored to the pin afterwards (git status clean).

Corroboration. Task 10-point validation check 7 (canonical-hidden) passed at this
same sealed hash on the host, so the mutation runner is functional by construction.
Splitting the batch by gate_type:
    solution        pilot (15 runs), W4 (17 runs)   -> hidden=pass on 32/32
    test_generation W1 (16 runs)                    -> hidden=fail on 15/15
The failure tracks the CODE PATH, not the task or the agent. check-hidden.sh has
two shapes; `solution` has the harness inject sealed tests into the subject tree,
while `test_generation` and `pr_review` exec a sealed runner (check.sh) with
SUBJECT_DIR exported. Only the second shape fails, and only in the container.

SCOPE — THIS IS NOT W1-ONLY. By gate_type, the executable-runner shape also covers
    W1b-zarr-block-mask-properties   test_generation
    W6-pr-review                     pr_review
so 3 of the 7 roster tasks are exposed. W4b and W3 are `solution` and unaffected on
this evidence. Expect the same false rejects on W1b and W6 in this pass.

Mechanism: NOT established. Two candidates, neither verified, recorded so the
post-batch investigation starts from evidence rather than a guess:
  (i)  the sealed set is bind-mounted READ-ONLY at <task>/hidden in the container;
       a runner that needs to write beside itself (dropping mutant files into
       place, intermediate output) would fail on that where the host run, with a
       writable directory, succeeds. The `solution` shape never writes into the
       sealed dir, which would explain why only one shape breaks.
  (ii) an environment difference in the gate image on the runner's exec path.
Testing (i) properly needs a read-only view of the sealed set, which cannot be
made without copying human-held material; it is left for the human. NO gate,
mount, or ceiling was changed in response to this finding.

Consequence, stated plainly:
  - The TELEMETRY of the W1 cells is unaffected and remains audit-grade valid.
    Tokens, cost, wall-clock, turns and identity are all real measurements.
  - The OUTCOME variable (acceptance.result) is WRONG for the affected cells and
    must not be read as a result, aggregated, or compared against any other task
    or arm. No acceptance rate may be computed over them.
  - The grade is RECOVERABLE OFFLINE at zero API cost: every run dir stores the
    agent's agent-solution.diff, and re-grading it takes ~2 minutes per run with no
    model call, exactly as done above. Re-grading is post-batch work and requires
    a decision from the human on whether a re-graded outcome may enter the dataset
    at all, or whether the affected cells become holes.
  - The batch therefore CONTINUES as instructed: W1, W1b and W6 cells still run.
    The spend buys valid telemetry and a recoverable grade, not a wasted cell.

