--- B. GATE-DISCOVERY DEFECT: diagnosis ----------------------------------------
Root cause, proven experimentally against the batch-1 images (not inferred):
the agent container writes into a named volume as uid 706335951 (lab); the gate
container mounts that same volume and runs as root. git then refuses the tree —
"fatal: detected dubious ownership in repository at '/subject'" — and EVERY git
call in the gate returns empty with rc=128. Sealed runners that DISCOVER the
agent's files via git therefore saw zero files and rejected.

  reproduce: gate image, as root, `git -C /subject ls-files --others` -> rc 128.
             same command with GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1 / safe.directory=/subject -> the
             agent's file, rc 0.
  fingerprint in batch 1: gate_type=solution (no git discovery) 32/32 hidden-pass;
             gate_type=test_generation (git discovery) 15/15 hidden-fail.
  corroboration: run.py's _archive_agent_diff_container() ALREADY passed that
             safe.directory env, which is exactly why every archived
             agent-solution.diff is intact while the gate saw nothing.

Fixed in harness/task-tools/lib.sh (git_trust_subject), wired into the G0/H0
readability checks. A tree git cannot read is now UNAVAILABLE (exit 2), never a
rejection. Regression test: tests/test_gate_subject_ownership.py (9 tests,
including a negative control that reproduces the pre-fix blind gate against the
real images).

