--- C. W6 FORENSIC: instrument error, not recall/precision ---------------------
Asked: are the W6 rejects genuine recall/precision failures, or a review-report
path/format problem? Answer: NEITHER, and the reason is upstream of both — the
participant was never given the artifact under review.

Evidence, per run (all 15 W6 runs re-graded; sealed-runner stderr in each run's
regrade-gate-hidden.log):
  1. sealed runner stderr, 15/15, verbatim:  "no review-report.txt — reject"
     (sealed-w6-v1 2026-08-17 k=6, hash sha256:350bf452...). The matcher never
     ran; there was no report to match against.
  2. agent-solution.diff is 0 bytes in 15/15 runs — nothing was written to the
     subject tree at all.
  3. task.yaml pins review_diff: hidden/review-diff.patch, which is SEALED and
     excluded from both images. invocation.txt shows the agent argv is
     `--print "<prompt>"` with NO diff appended: the prompt opens "Review the
     following diff" and no diff follows it.
  4. 12/15 agent stdouts say so in as many words ("There is no diff in your
     message"). 3 (C3-prev rep1/rep3, C3 rep2) produced defect lines inferred
     from the pristine source in the image; 2 (P0 rep1/rep2) are exit_code
     timeout with 0-byte stdout.
  5. Independently: the prompt never names an output path, while the sealed
     runner requires review-report.txt (harness/task-tools/validate.sh defaults
     review_report to that name; W6 task.yaml does not declare it). Even a run
     that HAD the diff would have written to stdout and been rejected.

Classification: MATERIAL-DELIVERY instrument error (primary) plus an undeclared
OUTPUT-CONTRACT defect (secondary). Two independent breaks, either one fatal.

Disposition: the offline re-grade was run over all 15 W6 runs and repairs
nothing — the archived output is stdout text produced without the diff, so there
is no artifact to re-grade. Grading those three source-derived guesses against a
defect map seeded into a diff the agent never saw would manufacture a number, not
recover one. W6 batch-1 cells are VOID (unscoreable), not "rejected", and a
re-run is spend and therefore out of scope for this pass. Both defects must be
fixed before any W6 makeup: deliver the sealed diff to the agent, and declare the
output path in the prompt.

